# a1_btpeval_shallowcopy
#
# donor      MOAI-GPU s1_complexroots_free (open arm). Mechanism: a read-only table that is a pure
#            function of the parameters exists in more copies than needed; make it one instance.
#            (Donor: 5,455 leaked copies of a root table; here 65 deep copies of the DFT matrices.)
#
# impl_lever: patch_shallowcopy.py
# The one source change of this step.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: btp.DeepCopyBootstrapEvaluator
# (Re-measured 2026-09-25, one run with in-run census; only the object key changed: first Arion/ frame
# (README.md), rank 1 at the re-measured a0 Arion/pkg/btp.DeepCopyBootstrapEvaluator, 274,786.8 MB; the
# leaf key below, ringqp.Ring.NewPoly, is the lattigo constructor underneath.)
# cost_class: free
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# basis      census: 210.6 GiB (38.8% of 542 GiB) under lintrans.NewLinearTransformation <-
#            dft.NewMatrixFromLiteral. Derived size of one pair (impl/derive_dft_size/):
#              CoeffsToSlots    93 polys x 34 limbs x 524,288 B = 1,657,798,656 B   1.54 GiB
#              SlotsToCoeffs   158 polys x 22 limbs x 524,288 B = 1,822,425,088 B   1.70 GiB
#              one evaluator                                      3,480,223,744 B   3.24 GiB
#              210.6 GiB measured / 3.24122 GiB derived = 64.98
#            65 copies (0.04% from 65).
# source     pkg/btp/matbtp.go:60, per-worker goroutine:
#     localBtpEval := DeepCopyBootstrapEvaluator(btpEval, btpParams) // 每个线程使用自己的 evaluator
#     // localBtpEval := btpEval.ShallowCopy()
#            DeepCopyBootstrapEvaluator (matbtp.go:89) -> bootstrapping.NewEvaluator rebuilds both sets
#            (evaluator.go:231,235). threads=64 + original = 65. Second site: pkg/bert/attentionMT.go:494.
#            ShallowCopy used at ~40 other places in the program.
# lever      ShallowCopy (evaluator.go:129: read-only structures shared, temporary buffers reallocated);
#            S2CDFTMatrix/C2SDFTMatrix shared, Evaluator/DFTEvaluator/Mod1Evaluator rebuilt.
# expected   210.6 -> 3.24 GiB (-207.4 GiB, ~38.2%); rlwe.NewEvaluatorBuffers (39.0 GiB) expected to stay.
# cost       declared free (n=1): removes 64 of 65 GenMatrices runs (251 polynomials per worker per
#            bootstrap). Risk: NUMA contention on one shared table.
# v1 failure job 45892530, 53 min, first bootstrap:
#                panic: level cannot be larger than max level
#                  ... dft.(*Evaluator).CoeffsToSlotsNew (dft.go:223)
#                  ... Arion/pkg/btp.CiphertextMatricesBootstrappingMT.func1 (matbtp.go:65)
#            lattigo v6.1.1 defect:
#              NewEvaluator  params := btpParams.BootstrappingParameters   evaluator.go:117, used at 121, 123
#              ShallowCopy   paramsN1 := eval.ResidualParameters           evaluator.go:133, used at 153, 154
#            DFT matrices at LevelQ = 29, residual parameters stop at 14 (reason for upstream's
#            commented-out line).
# v2         ShallowCopyBootstrapEvaluator (added to pkg/btp/matbtp.go): ShallowCopy, then rebuild the
#            two mis-parameterised fields with NewEvaluator's constructors and arguments.
# gate       compares decrypted output against the baseline (detects writes to the shared table).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# measured 2026-08-08, jobs 45896052 (clean), 45918456 (census):
#   peak      568,451,140 -> 322,689,788 kB   1.762x, -234.38 GiB, 43.2% of the peak
#   wall           23,333 -> 16,089 s         31% faster
#   gate T2   max_abs 1.84e-4 against a 1.5e-3 tolerance, an order of magnitude inside
# predicted 207.4 GiB, measured 234.4 GiB; surplus = evaluator buffers:
#   ringqp.Ring.NewPoly        326,687.2 -> 42,121.8 MB      the polynomial allocator, -278 GiB
#   rlwe.NewEvaluatorBuffers    39.0 GiB ->  ~2.1 GiB        `ckks.newEvaluatorBuffers` 1,556.6 MB
#                                                            plus `rlwe.NewEvaluatorBuffers` 561.5
# (bootstrapping.NewEvaluator allocated a full evaluator's RNS buffers 65 times.)
# rose:
#   rlwe.NewElement             52,429.6 -> 107,783.2 MB     +54 GiB
#   go:runtime_retained        158,041.5 -> 153,806.1 MB     flat in bytes, 0.272 -> 0.465 of peak
# runtime_retained now largest (Go analogue of MOAI-CPU's SEAL pool). NewElement rise: real or
# different snapshot phase (4.7% vs 3.2% below peak), not settled.
# a1_dft_one_at_a_time (paid; premise 65 pairs) moved off-path: one pair left, 1.54 GiB saving.
